```console
$ scherzo-cloud run input-set create --help
Create a Run Input Set

Usage: scherzo-cloud run input-set create [OPTIONS] --project-id <PROJECT> <ORGANIZATION>

Arguments:
  <ORGANIZATION>  Organization ID or exact slug

Options:
      --project-id <PROJECT>
          Project ID
      --input-text <NAME> <TEXT>
          Supply one required named Text value
      --input-text-file <NAME> <PATH|->
          Supply one required named Text value from a regular file, or - for standard input
      --input-json <NAME> <JSON>
          Supply one required named JSON value
      --input-json-file <NAME> <PATH|->
          Supply one required named JSON value from a regular file, or - for standard input
      --input-file <NAME> <MEDIA_TYPE> <PATH>
          Supply one required named File value with an explicit media type (maximum 64 MiB)
      --input-attachment <NAME> <MEDIA_TYPE> <PATH>
          Append an immutable member to a named attachment collection
      --input-attachments-empty <NAME>
          Supply a present named attachment collection with no members
      --json
          Print the run result as JSON
      --service-api-key-file <PATH|->
          Authenticate with a service API key from a private file, or - for standard input
      --allow-insecure-http
          Allow this command's Scherzo Cloud requests over insecure HTTP connections
  -h, --help
          Print help

Lifecycle:
  Creation fixes the manifest and each member's content. While open, the set accepts matching uploads; sealing verifies every declared member.

```
